// Cap token issuance at 10 per hour per user.
//
// Counts `IssueToken` responses in this user's recent history — the audit
// trail of tokens actually issued, not attempts. `count_within` is a
// built-in macro; the `exists` binder is how an aggregate is compared
// against a threshold.
//
// Enforcement is best-effort: audit writes on the login path are
// fire-and-forget, so a dropped write undercounts by one.
@id("issuance_rate_limit")
forbid (principal, action == Vouch::Action::"IssueToken", resource)
when temporal {
    exists (n: Long). (
        (count_within(1h, Vouch::Action::"IssueToken"::response{ callerPrincipal: principal })) == n
        && n >= 10
    )
};
